A FIFO named CLAUDE.md no longer hangs startup, and /add now refuses a FIFO, device or socket instead of hanging the REPL. This is only part of #1047: a FIFO at .yoyo/goal.md, .yoyo/memory.json or .yoyo.toml still hangs startup.

The repro you gave me (fresh git init dir, stdin /dev/null, mkfifo CLAUDE.md; timeout 10 yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG"):
• Before (cd3eb2d6): exit 124, no output at all.
• After: exit 0, stdout PONG, and stderr says ⚠ project instruction file CLAUDE.md not loaded — ./CLAUDE.md is not a regular file (FIFO): reading it could block forever or never end.

I then put a FIFO at each of the other auto-loaded names in turn. The other five instruction files (YOYO.md, AGENTS.md, .cursorrules, .yoyo/instructions.md, .github/copilot-instructions.md) all exit 0 now. The goal, memory and config files still exit 124. Fixing their readers would have taken the diff past the three files you scoped, so they're listed on the issue as the next slice.

What changed:
• `src/non_regular_read.rs`: two new shared readers, read_regular_to_string and a bytes version read_regular. Each first runs the existing file-type check, which follows symlinks and never opens the file, so it can't block. For anything that isn't a regular file it returns an error carrying the reason. The 4 new tests are here.
• `src/context.rs`: the startup loader and the /context///doctor listing now read through the new helper. A refused file is skipped with the existing yellow "not loaded" warning. The file grew from 2020 to 2029 lines, within its size grace.
• `src/commands_file.rs`: both /add readers (text and image) use the helper. The line count is unchanged at 2854.
• `docs/src/troubleshooting/common-issues.md`: now covers the two new readers and names the three files that still hang.

Tests: the new tests run each read on a thread with a 10-second timeout, so a regression fails by name instead of hanging the suite. They check that:
• a FIFO is refused quickly;
• a regular file and a symlink to one read back byte for byte;
• a FIFO CLAUDE.md is skipped while a regular AGENTS.md still loads;
• /add refuses a FIFO and still reads a normal file.

One test hung on its first run because of my own fixture: I passed the same lock as both the deny list and the allow list, and the code locks both at once, so it deadlocked. Production always passes two separate lists. The fixture now does too, with a comment saying why.

Positive control: with the loader temporarily switched back to a plain read, the loader test failed by name ("load_project_context_from hung on a FIFO"). It was restored in the same command and no marker is left. fmt, clippy with `-D warnings` and the full `cargo test` all pass.

